\f2\fs32 \cf0 I bet you ARE a good enough marketer to get promoted.
\f1\fs24 \

\f2\fs32 But, if your career is anything like mine, you\'92re not yet a good enough leader.
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f2\fs32 The penny dropped for me a few years ago. As Copy Club team grew I could sense that what was needed of me was changing fast. I couldn\'92t just do the work anymore. Instead, I needed to inspire others and set clear direction. \'93Taking charge\'94 felt unnatural because I just wanted to be one of the gang, but I realised it\'92s what the team & the business needed.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f2\fs32 At the risk of sounding like a motivational coach / faux guru, you just need to start seeing yourself as a leader and flexing those muscles.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f2\fs32 I\'92ve done a lot of reading, listening and thinking about leadership. I\'92ve realised it\'92s all about mindset.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f2\fs32 On Thursday I am giving a Copy Club talk on how to be a marketing leader. In 45 mins I am going to try to help you change your mindset.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f2\fs32 The talk is open to members and non-members as I think it\'92s too important to not spread far and wide. Please do forward on the link to your teams and friends. They might get something out of it and we\'92ll have a really lively Q&A if there is a big gang of us.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f2\fs32 Lottie x
\f1\fs24 \
\

\f2\fs32 PS. The talk will be available as a recording but just for members only. 
\f1\fs24 \
